# 2. Byte-string constants (continued). Each of these is a `br#"..."#`
# wire body fed to an API that takes `&[u8]` — `.to_vec()` into a
# response fixture, or `write_all` into the sink. `json!` yields a
# `Value`, so converting means `.to_string().into_bytes()` at every call
# site for no gain. The two `sink.rs` sites are also category 3: the
# assertion compares the accepted body against the exact bytes written.
crates/auctioneer-bidder/src/sink.rs 2

# 4. `format!` templates that SPLICE JSON text, and deliberately
# hostile structure. These build a nested chain of configurable depth
# and a configurable bid count to drive the node budget past its limit;
# `json!` cannot express a chain whose depth is a variable, and the
# over-limit cases are not valid input by design.
crates/auctioneer-bidder/tests/response_node_budget.rs 4
crates/auctioneer-exchange/tests/bidder_response_node_budget.rs 1

# Deliberately incomplete JSON verifies syntax-failure receipt consumption.
